---
title: Chicken, Pesto & Mozzarella Panini
course: main
cuisine: italian
servings: 2
time_active: 15
time_total: 20
leftovers: poor
tags: [lunch, quick]
pairs: [balsamic-brussels-sprouts]
---

Spread @pesto{1/4%cup} on one side of each slice of @ciabatta{4%slices}(or sourdough).

On two of the slices, layer @shredded chicken{1%cup}(rotisserie or leftover), @fresh mozzarella{1%cup}(sliced), @roasted red peppers{1/2%cup}(jarred, drained, and sliced), and @arugula{1/2%cup}. Top with the other slices, pesto side down.

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp}(or butter) in a #skillet{} over medium. Cook the panini ~{3-4%minutes} per side, pressing with a heavy pan, until the cheese melts and the bread is golden.

Slice diagonally and drizzle with @?balsamic glaze{1%tsp}.

> For more flavor, season the chicken with a pinch of smoked paprika or garlic powder before assembling.
